			"notes": "# Changelog\n\n## 1.0.0\n\nFirst release.\n\n- A game mode that confines you to a single chunk, with land bought outward one chunk at\n  a time. Enabled by a tick box on the Game tab when creating a world.\n- Locked chunks are hidden behind an electric haze. Touching the boundary hurts and throws\n  you back.\n- A phone in the inventory with three apps: a map for buying land, a counter for selling\n  goods, and a message list.\n- Prices derived from the world's own recipes, so every item is worth something and no\n  amount of crafting turns a profit.\n- Advancements pay out, graded by the game's own difficulty rating.\n- The Nether and the End hold their own territory, claimed on first arrival. Portals into\n  land you do not own will not fire."
		}
